      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1op3tqr'
    male|a||Among a hundred winners, forty-six have one. Among a hundred losers, thirty-four.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:e22uqa'
    'male|a||Winners minus losers, everyone counted as drawn: twelve percentage points. That is the intention-to-treat effect.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:12s4mfu'
    male|b||But seventy of those winners never got covered. Isn't the twelve simply wrong?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; steady, lively pace, never slow #ctx:4j1el1'
    'male|a||Not wrong: diluted. Only chance decided who won, so the whole twelve points is caused by winning.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:19ms6l6'
    male|a||It is the effect of the offer, averaged over everyone who got one, most of whom never used it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1siqnbl'
    male|b||Then if only thirty people moved, their own gain must be far bigger than twelve.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4760
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; steady, lively pace, never slow #ctx:173jrio'
    male|a||That is the number we are after. And there is a tempting shortcut to it, right here among the winners.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:wl5r30'
    male|a||Here is the shortcut. Among the winners we can see exactly who enrolled, so why not compare them with the winners who stayed out?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8200
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Write Y of one for a person's outcome with coverage, and Y of zero without. Sixty percent of the enrolled have a regular clinic; forty percent of those who stayed out.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1xgx24k'
    male|b||A twenty-point gap, and still inside a randomized experiment. What could be wrong with that?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6160
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; steady, lively pace, never slow #ctx:h34pvz'
    'male|a||The lottery decided who was drawn. It did not decide who enrolled: the winners decided that themselves.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1g7pyu4'
    male|a||And in Oregon, those who enrolled because they won were older, poorer and in worse health than the lottery's entrants as a whole, so worse off than the winners who stayed out.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1xt6gob'
    'male|b||Before we look inside the table: The enrolled were poorer and sicker than the winners who stayed out, and less likely to have a regular clinic on their own. So the twenty-point gap is…':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; steady, lively pace, never slow #ctx:l985nt'
    'male|b||Smaller: without coverage the enrolled would have been further behind the others, so comparing them with the others understates what coverage did.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; steady, lively pace, never slow'
    'male|a||Fill in the cell the data never show: the enrolled winners'' share with a clinic, had they stayed uncovered.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7320
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Poorer and sicker, say they would have had one only twenty percent of the time. That twenty is made up, like all our example's numbers.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:5fvvfi'
    'male|a||So coverage lifted them from twenty to sixty. That gap is the effect, tau: forty points.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1cc812t'
    male|b||Then the shortcut's twenty finds only half of it. Where did the other twenty go?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5080
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; steady, lively pace, never slow #ctx:wnbmgp'
    male|a||Split the gap in two, by adding and taking away the enrolled group's twenty.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:oodjfz'
    'male|a||The first piece, sixty minus twenty, is what coverage did for the enrolled: forty points.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:18rvmsp'
    'male|a||The second compares two groups who are both uncovered, so it measures who they are, not what they got: minus twenty. That is selection bias.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:h04koa'
    male|a||Forty points of effect, minus twenty points of selection, and the shortcut shows twenty.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:va57uh'
    male|b||So once we split the winners by what they chose, the lottery stops protecting us?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; steady, lively pace, never slow #ctx:pm4txz'
    'male|a||Completely. Oregon''s team saw it in their own data: compare the covered with the uncovered, and insurance even seemed to make people''s health worse.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1f4zcjo'
    male|a||The draw's two groups were never split by choice, so on average each holds the same mix of people. That is where the honest forty is hiding.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:115jrby'
    'male|a||Back to the honest comparison, winners against losers. Its twelve points come from a mix: thirty winners in a hundred who enrolled because they won, gaining on average tau-bar, and seventy who never would.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13840
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||For those seventy, winning changed nothing: no coverage, so no effect. They add zero.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1gc77en'
    male|b||How do you know winning did nothing for them? They did get a letter from the state.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4120
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; steady, lively pace, never slow #ctx:fd7x91'
    'male|a||We don''t know it; we assume it. Economists call it the exclusion restriction: the draw may matter only through coverage, and a letter alone is unlikely to give anyone a clinic.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1y3npl5'
    male|a||So the whole twelve comes from the thirty who moved.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 3480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1b1bhjz'
    'male|a||Divide by their share: on average, forty points each, the hidden number from inside the table.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:6m95e0'
    male|b||So the lottery's twelve was the forty, watered down by everyone who stayed away.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5600
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; steady, lively pace, never slow #ctx:1n2n5y8'
    'male|a||In general: the gap in outcomes between winners and losers, divided by the gap in coverage. It is called the LATE, the local average treatment effect: the average effect for compliers, the people the draw moved.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1xbg39'
    male|a||In our example no loser got covered, so the people the draw moved are exactly the enrolled winners, and the LATE is their effect.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:129ulem'
    'male|a||The division leans on four things: the draw is random, it moves coverage at all, it matters only through coverage, and it pushes nobody out of coverage.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:lko2ks'
    male|a||Now suppose the effect on the people the draw moves stayed at forty, however many it moved.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:moaogg'
    'male|a||Then the lottery''s comparison would show forty times the extra coverage: at thirty points, twelve.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1qsmhl5'
    male|a||Watch the point slide from everyone enrolling down to almost no one, and the gap between the lines.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:3ci3hg'
    male|a||At full take-up the two numbers meet. As take-up falls, the lottery's number shrinks toward zero, while the effect, held still by assumption, stays at forty.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12320
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Oregon's real numbers sit on the same picture. Some losers found Medicaid another way, so the extra coverage from winning, among those surveyed, was about twenty-nine points.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:98j95'
    male|a||Winners were about ten points more likely to have a regular clinic, give or take one and a half.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:9v82z4'
    'male|a||Divided by twenty-nine, that is about thirty-four for those the lottery moved, give or take five: far too large to be chance.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1iwf76x'
    'male|a||The same division works for how people felt: about four points more winners called their health good or better, give or take one and a half, which is about thirteen for those the lottery moved, give or take five.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:18b1u23'
    male|a||So one lottery gives two honest numbers, twelve and forty. Which should a report lead with?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6000
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|b||The forty, surely. The twelve is just the forty, damaged by people who never showed up.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; steady, lively pace, never slow #ctx:ly9w4i'
    'male|a||Not damaged: it answers another question. Twelve is what the state gets per invitation, with take-up as people really behave.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:bpwei6'
    male|a||So a state deciding whether to run its lottery again, or budgeting per name drawn, wants the twelve.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:184favl'
    'male|a||Forty is what coverage does for the people who take it up when offered: a question about the insurance itself.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:42qm0a'
    male|b||Then a state with better outreach could expect forty times its own take-up?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; steady, lively pace, never slow #ctx:1t8c8o4'
    'male|a||Only if its new enrollees resemble Oregon''s. The forty belongs to the people this lottery moved: poorer, sicker, and organised enough to send back the forms.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1eqx436'
    male|a||People pulled in by a harder push might gain more, or less, and this lottery cannot tell us which.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:165fb2a'
    male|a||Economists argue over such local numbers. Critics such as James Heckman and Angus Deaton say it is tied to one lottery and one group of people; Guido Imbens replies that a credible local answer beats a general guess.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 15520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:pm083a'
    'male|a||What would settle it is the effect measured at other margins: a different push that moves different people, compared with this one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:nvga42'
    male|a||Medicine chose its default long ago. The drug regulators' trial guideline, known as E9, from 1998, puts the analysis by assignment first.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:q4hzrp'
    male|a||A pill that patients abandon helps no one, and analysing everyone as randomized keeps the comparison fair.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:hj5ccz'
    male|a||Try it on four questions people actually ask.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 3680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:7sbbls'
    male|a||Which number answers each question? Drag each card to its number.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:d6rkzb'
    male|a||Questions about the policy as delivered want the twelve. Questions about what insurance does want the forty, and only for someone like the people the lottery moved.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10480
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|b||One new trial. A clinic offers free nicotine patches to a random half of its smokers; nobody else gets them. Only half of those offered use them. A year on, 20% of those offered have quit, against 14% of the rest. What did the patches do for those who used them?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 18600
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; steady, lively pace, never slow #ctx:101v1sn'
    'male|b||About twelve: the six-point gap from the offer, divided by the half who actually used the patches.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; steady, lively pace, never slow'
    'male|a||So what does comparing Oregon''s winners with its losers measure? The effect of being offered Medicaid: honest, and diluted.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8800
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Splitting the winners by who enrolled throws the lottery away, because enrolling was a choice.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1uwydqs'
    male|a||And dividing by the gap in coverage brings back the effect of insurance itself, for the people the lottery moved.:
